H2('E. Integral Cryptanalysis')
P("Qo‘sh destroys byte-level integral properties after one application because J and K depend on all elements. Bit-level properties, however, persist: if one state byte takes all 256 values, its LSB takes each value 128 times, and by Lemma 1 every output LSB is a linear function of input LSBs, so all 32 LSBs remain balanced. Experiments with 40 random keys confirm that the LSB layer is balanced with probability 1 after each of rounds 1–7 and loses balance at the absorption in round 8 (Fig. @F:int). In the 128-bit mode the property survives all absorptions, giving a 32-bit integral distinguisher on the full hash with 16 (one active nibble) or 256 chosen messages.")
